---
import BankLogo from '../components/BankLogo.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import data from '../data/banks.json';
import {bankFreshness} from '../lib/bank-freshness.mjs';
import {savings} from '../lib/finance.mjs';
const illustration=(rate:number)=>savings({principal:10000,contribution:0,frequency:'monthly',annualRate:rate,years:1}).interest;
const dollars=(value:number)=>new Intl.NumberFormat('en-AU',{style:'currency',currency:'AUD'}).format(value);
const count=data.banks.reduce((sum,b)=>sum+b.productCount,0);
const date=new Date(data.fetchedAt).toLocaleDateString('en-AU',{timeZone:'Australia/Brisbane',day:'numeric',month:'long',year:'numeric'});
---
<Base title="Australian bank product explorer" description="Find Australian banking brands, see published deposit products and conditions, and try their supported base rates in a savings calculator.">
<header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Bank rates</div><h1>Find your bank’s rates.</h1><p>Choose a bank to explore its products and calculate your savings.</p></header>
<div class="hl-wrap hl-page-main">
<p style="margin-bottom:24px"><a class="hl-button" href="/compare/savings/">Compare savings interest in dollars →</a></p>
<div class="hl-bank-search"><label class="hl-field"><span>Search banks</span><input class="hl-search" type="search" id="bank-filter" placeholder="Bank name, e.g. CommBank or ING" aria-label="Search banks"/></label><label class="bank-availability"><input type="checkbox" id="bank-show-unavailable"/> Include brands with no deposit data</label><p class="hl-help" id="bank-count" aria-live="polite">{data.banks.filter(b=>b.productCount>0).length} brands with deposit data · Alphabetical order</p><p class="hl-help">Bank feeds checked weekly · Latest refresh: {date}. Each bank shows its own retrieval date. Confirm current terms with the bank.</p></div>
<details class="hl-details"><summary>Coverage, rate conditions & sources</summary><p>{count} deposit and transaction products retrieved. This directory covers brands in the CDR register, not every bank or product. Some feeds are incomplete or unavailable. Listings are not recommendations.</p><section class="hl-bank-reading"><h2>Read the account, not just the percentage.</h2><p>A useful comparison starts with the amount you will actually keep in an account, whether you can meet its conditions and what it costs. These listings are a starting point for your own checks.</p><ol><li><strong>Check access and eligibility.</strong> A transaction, restricted or offset account may not work like a general savings account.</li><li><strong>Separate the rate components.</strong> Base, bonus and introductory rates are different. Do not add them together unless the provider confirms that is how the offer works.</li><li><strong>Check time, balance caps and fees.</strong> A rate may apply only to part of a balance or only for a short period. A small fee can outweigh a modest rate increase.</li></ol>
<details class="hl-year-table"><summary>A worked comparison: when the higher rate leaves less money</summary><p>Two hypothetical accounts start with $10,000, no deposits or withdrawals and monthly compounding for one year. Account A pays 4.0% with no fee. Account B pays 4.6% with a $120 fee paid at the end of the year. These are teaching examples, not bank offers.</p><div class="hl-table-scroll"><table class="hl-table"><caption>One-year illustration before tax</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Account</th><th scope="col">Interest</th><th scope="col">Annual fee</th><th scope="col">Interest less fee</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">A · 4.0%</th><td>{dollars(illustration(4))}</td><td>$0.00</td><td>{dollars(illustration(4))}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">B · 4.6%</th><td>{dollars(illustration(4.6))}</td><td>$120.00</td><td>{dollars(illustration(4.6)-120)}</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Here, the higher-rate account leaves {dollars(illustration(4)-(illustration(4.6)-120))} less after the fee. Different balances, fee timing or bonus eligibility could change the comparison. Our savings calculator excludes fees, so compare costs separately.</p></details>
<p><a href="/learn/bonus-interest-conditions">Understand bonus rates and conditions →</a> · <a href="/methodology">How the data and calculations work →</a></p></section><div class="hl-explainer"><div><h2>Public product data. No account access.</h2><p>We retrieve product information from the public APIs listed in the Australian Government’s Consumer Data Right register. These describe products and their terms; they contain no customer balances or transactions.</p><p>Snapshots show a retrieval date. The calculator can automatically model simple base variable rates and supported dollar-based tiers. Where the feed has an unambiguous bonus or a welcome period measured in whole months or years, you can compare a separate scenario after confirming the conditions. It never decides whether you qualify. Welcome periods return to the base rate at the end; unsupported combinations remain separate.</p></div><div><h2>Where the information comes from</h2><p><a href="https://www.cdr.gov.au/for-providers/how-find-data-holders-product-data-request-service">CDR: public product data ↗</a></p><p><a href="https://www.apra.gov.au/registers/list-registered-authorised-deposit-taking-institutions">APRA: authorised institutions ↗</a></p><p><a href="/methodology">Our coverage and rate methodology →</a></p></div></div></details>
<div class="hl-bank-grid">{data.banks.map(b=><a class="hl-bank-row" data-bank-name={b.name.toLowerCase()} data-has-products={b.productCount>0?'true':'false'} hidden={b.productCount===0} href={'/calculators/compound-interest/?bank='+b.id}><BankLogo id={b.id} /><div><h2>{b.name}</h2><small>{b.productCount+(b.productCount===1?' product':' products')} · {bankFreshness(b).date ? 'Retrieved '+bankFreshness(b).date : 'No retrieval recorded'}{b.status==='partial'?' · partial data':b.status!=='available'?' · refresh needed':''}</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>)}</div>
<p id="bank-empty" class="hl-empty" hidden>No matching provider with these filters. Try including brands without data, or <a href="/calculators/compound-interest">enter your own interest rate</a>.</p>
</div></Base>
<script>
const input=document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#bank-filter')!;
const cards=[...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-bank-name]')];
const normalise=(s:string)=>s.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g,'');
const aliases:Record<string,string>={commonwealth:'commbank',commonwealthbank:'commbank',cba:'commbank',nab:'nationalaustraliabank'};
const unavailable=document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#bank-show-unavailable')!;
const filter=()=>{const typed=normalise(input.value.trim());const query=aliases[typed]||typed;let count=0;cards.forEach(card=>{const name=normalise(card.dataset.bankName||'');const show=(unavailable.checked||card.dataset.hasProducts==='true')&&(name.includes(typed)||name.includes(query));card.hidden=!show;if(show)count++;});document.querySelector('#bank-count')!.textContent=count+(count===1?' banking brand':' banking brands')+(typed?' found':' · Alphabetical order');(document.querySelector('#bank-empty') as HTMLElement).hidden=count!==0;};
input.addEventListener('input',filter);unavailable.addEventListener('change',filter);filter();
</script>

